{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the cloud covered him.</b> Our Sages disagree in the matter. Some say: these are six days from the New Moon — until the festival, the day of the giving of the Torah." "<b>And the cloud covered him.</b> The mountain." "<b>And He called to Moses on the seventh day</b> — to speak the Ten Commandments, and Moses and all the children of Israel were standing, but Scripture divided the honor to Moses. And some say: <b>And the cloud covered</b> Moses <b>six days</b> — after the Ten Commandments, and these were at the beginning of the forty days that Moses went up to receive the tablets. And this teaches you that all who enter the camp of the Shechinah require separation for six days (Yoma 3)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:20.384833766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}